  "introduction": "The Bible says He is near to the brokenhearted and saves those who are crushed in spirit. Where do you most need the Holy Spirit's comfort right now? (Psalm 34:18) How could God use your past pain to help someone else? (2 Corinthians 1:3-11) We are becoming more like Jesus for the sake of others. When you come to church, do you come primarily to be filled, or to worship God and encourage others? (Mark 10:45) What next step could help you live more intentionally in that direction? Is it joining a Crew, starting to serve, or talking to someone new today? What gift, talent, or strength has God given you that could encourage or build up someone else this week? Ask the Holy Spirit to bring a specific person to mind, then intentionally use that gift to be a blessing to them. (Romans 12:3-8)",
